---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Layout
    title="Privacy Policy | BatteryTrail"
    description="How BatteryTrail collects, uses, and protects your information, including advertising cookies and analytics."
>
    <Header />

    <main class="flex-grow w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
        <div class="mb-10 border-b border-[#224249] pb-8">
            <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white leading-[1.15]">
                Privacy Policy
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-text-muted">
                Last updated: {lastUpdated}
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline">
            <p>
                BatteryTrail ("we", "our", or "us") operates the website located
                at <a href="https://www.batterytrail.com">https://www.batterytrail.com</a>
                (the "Site"). This Privacy Policy explains what information we
                collect, how we use it, and the choices you have about it. By
                using the Site, you agree to the practices described here.
            </p>

            <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>
                We collect information in a few limited ways:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Information you provide.</strong> If you contact us by
                    email, we receive the contents of your message and your email
                    address, which we use only to respond to you.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Automatically collected information.</strong> Like most
                    websites, we may automatically receive standard technical
                    information when you visit, such as your browser type, device
                    type, approximate location (derived from IP address), pages
                    visited, and the referring site. This is collected through
                    analytics and advertising services described below.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Cookies and similar technologies.</strong> We and our
                    partners use cookies, web beacons, and similar technologies.
                    See our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
            <p>
                We use the information we collect to operate and improve the Site,
                understand how visitors use our content, measure performance, and
                serve and personalize advertising. We do not sell your personal
                information.
            </p>

            <h2>Advertising (Google AdSense and Third-Party Cookies)</h2>
            <p>
                We may display advertisements on the Site through Google AdSense
                and other third-party advertising partners. These providers use
                cookies and similar technologies to serve ads based on your prior
                visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising
                cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on
                your visit to our Site and other sites on the Internet.
            </p>
            <p>
                You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
                <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
                You can also opt out of many third-party advertising networks by
                visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Analytics</h2>
            <p>
                We use analytics services (such as Google Analytics or a similar
                platform) to understand aggregate usage of the Site, such as which
                pages are most visited and how visitors reach us. These services
                may set cookies and collect anonymized usage data.
            </p>

            <h2>Legal Bases and Your Rights</h2>
            <h3>GDPR (European Economic Area and UK)</h3>
            <p>
                If you are located in the European Economic Area or the United
                Kingdom, you have the right to access, correct, delete, or
                restrict the processing of your personal data, and to object to
                certain processing. To exercise these rights, contact us using the
                details below.
            </p>
            <h3>CCPA / CPRA (California)</h3>
            <p>
                If you are a California resident, you have the right to request
                disclosure of the categories and specific pieces of personal
                information we collect, and to request deletion of your personal
                information, subject to legal exceptions. We do not sell your
                personal information. To make a request, contact us using the
                details below.
            </p>

            <h2>Data Retention and Security</h2>
            <p>
                We retain information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the
                purposes described in this policy or as required by law. We use
                reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to
                protect the information we hold. No method of transmission over the
                Internet is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute
                security.
            </p>

            <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>
                The Site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not
                knowingly collect personal information from children. If you
                believe a child has provided us with personal information, please
                contact us and we will delete it.
            </p>

            <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
            <p>
                The Site contains links to third-party websites and products. We
                are not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites. We
                encourage you to review their privacy policies.
            </p>

            <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last
                updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent
                revision. Continued use of the Site after changes are posted
                constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
            </p>

            <h2>Contact Us</h2>
            <p>
                If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise
                your rights, contact us at
                <a href="mailto:chesterbeard@salishseaconsulting.com">chesterbeard@salishseaconsulting.com</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
</Layout>
